const CAR_ROWS = [
    ["Aston Martin DB4 GT Zagato","Aston Martin",1960,"GB","gt","3.7-litre straight-six",314,153,6.1,1225,19,"A lighter, sleeker DB4 GT with a hand-made aluminium body from the Italian design house Zagato. It was built to race against the Ferrari 250 GT, and today it is one of the most valuable Aston Martins in the world.","Zagato's designer Ercole Spada was only in his twenties when he drew it.","Aston Martin planned 25 cars, but only 19 were made in the 1960s.","I am a British GT with an Italian body by Zagato, and only 19 of me were built in the 1960s.","Aston Martin DB4 GT Zagato"],
    ["Jaguar E-Type","Jaguar",1961,"GB","sports","3.8-litre straight-six",265,150,6.9,1234,70000,"When the E-Type was shown at the Geneva Motor Show in 1961 people could hardly believe it: it looked like a racing car, could reach 150 mph, and cost far less than a Ferrari. Its long bonnet hides a straight-six engine.","Its shape was drawn by Malcolm Sayer, an aircraft engineer who used maths and wind ideas from planes.","More than 70,000 were built between 1961 and 1974.","I am the British sports car with a super-long bonnet that wowed Geneva in 1961.","Jaguar E-Type"],
    ["AC Shelby Cobra","AC Cars",1962,"GB","sports","7.0-litre V8 (Ford)",425,164,null,916,998,"American racer Carroll Shelby took a light British sports car, the AC Ace, and squeezed a big Ford V8 engine into it. The result was the Cobra: tiny, loud and brutally fast. The later 427 version had a 7-litre engine.","Cobras beat Ferrari to win the World Sportscar Championship GT class in 1965.","Lots of companies still build Cobra replicas, because the originals are so rare and valuable.","I am a small British car with a huge American V8, made famous by Carroll Shelby.","AC Cobra"],
    ["Bentley S3 Continental","Bentley",1962,"GB","gt","6.2-litre V8",null,113,null,1918,null,"A big, luxurious British coupé that could cruise fast and quietly all day. Bodies were hand-built by coachbuilders, and its 6.2-litre V8 was made by Rolls-Royce, which owned Bentley then.","Bentley would not say how powerful the engine was. The official answer was 'adequate'.","It has four headlights stacked in pairs, a style of the 1960s.","When people asked how powerful my V8 was, the answer was simply 'adequate'.","Bentley S3"],
    ["Ferrari 250 GTO","Ferrari",1962,"IT","homologation","3.0-litre V12",296,174,5.6,880,36,"A racing car you could drive on the road. The 250 GTO won the world championship for GT cars three years in a row (1962, 1963 and 1964). Only 36 were made, and it is now one of the most expensive cars ever sold.","GTO stands for Gran Turismo Omologato, Italian for 'homologated grand tourer'.","The rules said 100 had to be built, but Ferrari persuaded the officials to accept far fewer.","I am the 1960s Ferrari racer that sells for tens of millions, and only 36 of me exist.","Ferrari 250 GTO"],
    ["Lotus Elan","Lotus",1962,"GB","sports","1.6-litre four-cylinder",105,114,8.7,640,12224,"Colin Chapman's little Lotus Elan was light, nimble and fun. It had a strong steel backbone chassis with a glass-fibre body on top, and it handled so well that other car makers studied it.","The Elan weighed about as much as three grand pianos, very light for a car.","Engineers at Mazda said the Elan inspired their MX-5 roadster in 1989.","I am Colin Chapman's tiny 1960s sports car with a glass-fibre body and a backbone chassis.","Lotus Elan"],
    ["Aston Martin DB5","Aston Martin",1963,"GB","gt","4.0-litre straight-six",282,145,8,1502,1059,"The most famous Aston Martin of all. The DB5 was a fast, elegant grand tourer, built to cross countries in comfort. Then James Bond drove one in the 1964 film Goldfinger, and it became a movie legend.","The letters DB come from David Brown, the businessman who owned Aston Martin.","Bond's film car had gadgets like an ejector seat and machine guns behind the indicators.","James Bond drove me in Goldfinger, complete with an ejector seat.","Aston Martin DB5"],
    ["Lola Mk6","Lola",1963,"GB","race","4.2-litre V8 (Ford)",null,null,null,null,3,"A small British racing coupé designed by Eric Broadley. It used a Ford V8 engine in the middle of the car and impressed everyone at Le Mans in 1963. Ford liked it so much that it became the starting point for the GT40.","Only three Lola Mk6 cars were built.","Eric Broadley worked with Ford in England while the first GT40s were designed.","I am Eric Broadley's racing car that Ford used as the starting point for the GT40.","Lola Mk6"],
    ["Ford GT40","Ford",1964,"US","race","4.2-litre V8",371,null,null,null,105,"Ford built the GT40 to beat Ferrari at the Le Mans 24 Hours, after Enzo Ferrari refused to sell his company to Ford. It worked: GT40s won Le Mans four times in a row, from 1966 to 1969.","It is called GT40 because it is only 40 inches (about 1 metre) tall.","In 1966, GT40s finished first, second and third at Le Mans.","I was built to beat Ferrari at Le Mans, and I am only 40 inches tall.","Ford GT40"],
    ["Lamborghini 350 GT","Lamborghini",1964,"IT","gt","3.5-litre V12",270,158,6.8,1450,120,"The very first Lamborghini road car. Ferruccio Lamborghini made tractors, and he wanted to build a grand tourer that was smoother and better made than a Ferrari. The 350 GT had a 3.5-litre V12 engine.","It was shown at the Geneva Motor Show in March 1964.","Only 120 were built before it was replaced by the 400 GT.","I am the first Lamborghini road car, built by a tractor maker.","Lamborghini 350 GT"],
    ["Porsche 911","Porsche",1964,"DE","sports","2.0-litre flat-six",128,131,9.1,1080,null,"The 911 first went on sale in 1964 and it has been made ever since, always with its engine at the back. The early cars had an air-cooled flat-six engine and a shape that is still recognisable today.","It was first going to be called the 901, but the car maker Peugeot used names with a 0 in the middle.","The shape was drawn by Ferdinand Alexander 'Butzi' Porsche, grandson of the company's founder.","I nearly had the name 901, and I've been made with my engine at the back since 1964.","Porsche 911 (classic)"],
    ["Lamborghini Miura","Lamborghini",1966,"IT","supercar","3.9-litre V12",345,171,6.7,1292,764,"Many people call the Miura the first supercar. Its V12 engine sat sideways behind the driver, like a racing car, and its low, curvy body by Marcello Gandini at Bertone stunned the world. It was the fastest production car of its time.","Lamborghini's young engineers designed it in their spare time.","It is named after a famous breeder of Spanish fighting bulls, Don Eduardo Miura.","I am often called the very first supercar, with a V12 sideways behind the seats.","Lamborghini Miura"],
    ["Alfa Romeo 33 Stradale","Alfa Romeo",1967,"IT","supercar","2.0-litre V8",227,160,null,700,18,"A racing car made legal for the road: 'Stradale' means 'road-going' in Italian. It had a tiny 2.0-litre V8 that revved very high, doors that open upwards, and one of the most beautiful shapes ever, by Franco Scaglione.","Only 18 were built between 1967 and 1969.","In 2023 Alfa Romeo made a new 33 Stradale in its honour.","I am a 1960s Alfa Romeo racer for the road, with butterfly doors, and only 18 of me were made.","Alfa Romeo 33 Stradale"],
    ["De Tomaso Mangusta","De Tomaso",1967,"IT","supercar","4.7-litre V8 (Ford)",306,155,null,1300,401,"An Italian supercar with an American Ford V8 in the middle. Its body was drawn by Giorgetto Giugiaro, and its engine cover opens like a pair of gull wings.","'Mangusta' means mongoose in Italian, an animal that can beat a cobra.","Its name was a cheeky joke aimed at Carroll Shelby's Cobra.","My name means mongoose, because a mongoose can beat a cobra.","De Tomaso Mangusta"],
    ["Maserati Ghibli","Maserati",1967,"IT","gt","4.7-litre V8",306,154,6.8,null,1295,"A long, low grand tourer with a V8 engine at the front and a huge fuel tank for crossing continents. Giorgetto Giugiaro drew its sharp shape when he was still in his twenties.","Like many Maseratis, it is named after a wind: the Ghibli is a hot desert wind.","A Spyder version with a folding roof was also made.","I am a 1960s Maserati named after a hot desert wind.","Maserati Ghibli"],
    ["Toyota 2000GT","Toyota",1967,"JP","gt","2.0-litre straight-six",148,135,null,1120,351,"The car that showed the world Japan could build a true sports car. Toyota made it together with Yamaha, who built the cars. It had a 2.0-litre straight-six engine, and only 351 were made.","Two open-top versions were made for the James Bond film You Only Live Twice.","Its dashboard was made of wood by Yamaha, who also made pianos.","I am a rare Japanese sports car built by Yamaha, and I appeared in a James Bond film.","Toyota 2000GT"],
    ["Ferrari Daytona","Ferrari",1968,"IT","gt","4.4-litre V12",347,174,5.4,1200,1406,"A front-engined V12 grand tourer, fast enough to rival the mid-engined Miura. Its official name is 365 GTB/4, but everyone calls it Daytona after Ferrari's 1-2-3 finish at the Daytona 24 Hours race in 1967.","A pretend Daytona was the hero car in the TV series Miami Vice.","Early cars had headlights under a clear cover; later ones had pop-up lights.","I am a front-engined V12 Ferrari named after a 1-2-3 win in Florida.","Ferrari Daytona"],
    ["Mercedes-Benz 300 SEL 6.3","Mercedes-Benz",1968,"DE","gt","6.3-litre V8",247,137,6.5,1780,6526,"A big, comfortable family saloon with a secret: a huge 6.3-litre V8 from Mercedes' grand limousine. It could outrun many sports cars, which made it one of the first 'super saloons'.","An engineer named Erich Waxenberger built the first one on his own, without permission.","It had air suspension to give a smooth ride.","I look like a sensible saloon car, but I hide a giant 6.3-litre V8.","Mercedes-Benz W108/W109"],
    ["Dino 246 GT","Ferrari",1969,"IT","sports","2.4-litre V6",192,146,null,1080,null,"Enzo Ferrari named the Dino after his son Alfredo 'Dino' Ferrari, who died young. The Dino was smaller and cheaper than other Ferraris, with a V6 engine behind the driver, and it is loved for how sweetly it drives.","The early Dinos did not wear a Ferrari badge: Dino was sold as its own brand.","The 246 was the first Ferrari-made car built in large numbers.","I am named after Enzo Ferrari's son, and I have a V6 instead of a V12.","Dino 206 GT and 246 GT"],
    ["Mercedes-Benz C111","Mercedes-Benz",1969,"DE","concept","4-rotor Wankel engine",345,186,null,null,16,"An orange experimental car that Mercedes used to test new ideas, like the Wankel rotary engine (which spins instead of pumping up and down) and later diesel and turbo engines. It had gull-wing doors.","Diesel versions set world speed records in the 1970s.","Rich customers sent blank cheques asking to buy one, but Mercedes never sold it.","I am an orange Mercedes test car with gull-wing doors and a spinning rotary engine.","Mercedes-Benz C111"],
    ["Porsche 917","Porsche",1969,"DE","race","4.9-litre flat-12",592,224,null,800,null,"One of the greatest racing cars ever. Its flat-12 engine was huge and powerful, and it gave Porsche its first overall Le Mans win in 1970, then again in 1971. Later turbo versions had over 1,000 horsepower.","Porsche had to build 25 of them before they were allowed to race, a big gamble in 1969.","The 917 starred in the Steve McQueen film Le Mans.","I gave Porsche its first overall Le Mans win, in 1970.","Porsche 917"],
    ["De Tomaso Pantera","De Tomaso",1971,"IT","supercar","5.8-litre V8 (Ford)",326,159,5.5,1420,7260,"An Italian body with an American heart. The Pantera had a 5.8-litre Ford V8 in the middle and was sold in Ford's American Lincoln-Mercury dealers. It stayed in production for over 20 years.","'Pantera' means panther in Italian.","More than 7,000 were made, a big number for an Italian supercar.","I am an Italian panther with an American Ford V8, sold by Ford dealers.","De Tomaso Pantera"],
    ["Maserati Bora","Maserati",1971,"IT","supercar","4.7-litre V8",306,165,6.5,1535,564,"Maserati's first mid-engined road car, with a V8 behind the seats. It was more comfortable than most supercars, with a quiet cabin, a big boot at the front and pedals that move to fit the driver.","It is named after the Bora, a cold wind that blows across the Adriatic Sea.","Giorgetto Giugiaro designed the shape with a brushed steel roof.","I am the first mid-engined Maserati road car, named after a cold wind.","Maserati Bora"],
    ["Ferrari 365 GT4 BB","Ferrari",1973,"IT","supercar","4.4-litre flat-12",355,188,5.4,1235,387,"The first mid-engined Ferrari with 12 cylinders. The 'BB' stands for Berlinetta Boxer: its flat-12 engine has pistons that punch outwards like boxers' fists. It was Ferrari's answer to the Countach.","Its shape was drawn by Leonardo Fioravanti at Pininfarina.","It replaced the front-engined Daytona in 1973.","My engine's pistons punch outwards like boxers, which is why I'm called BB.","Ferrari Berlinetta Boxer"],
    ["Lancia Stratos","Lancia",1973,"IT","homologation","2.4-litre V6 (Ferrari)",187,143,6.8,980,492,"A car built purely to win rallies. It is very short and wide, with a Ferrari V6 engine behind the driver. It won the World Rally Championship in 1974, 1975 and 1976.","About 492 road cars were built so that it was allowed to compete.","Its wedge shape came from Marcello Gandini at Bertone.","I am a short, wedge-shaped rally car with a Ferrari engine that won three world titles.","Lancia Stratos"],
    ["Lamborghini Countach","Lamborghini",1974,"IT","supercar","3.9-litre V12",370,179,5.6,1300,1999,"The ultimate 1970s poster car. Marcello Gandini's wedge shape was sharp, low and wild, and the doors swing up like scissors. A V12 sits behind the driver. It was made from 1974 to 1990.","Its name comes from a word of amazement in the Piedmont dialect of Italy.","Visibility was so poor that drivers reversed by sitting on the door sill and looking back.","I am the 1970s wedge with scissor doors that was on every bedroom wall.","Lamborghini Countach"],
    ["Ferrari 308 GTB","Ferrari",1975,"IT","supercar","2.9-litre V8",252,157,6.5,1090,null,"A small V8 Ferrari with a gorgeous Pininfarina shape. The very first cars had glass-fibre bodies to save weight. It became one of Ferrari's best-selling cars of the 1970s and 80s.","A red 308 GTS (the open version) was the star car of the TV series Magnum, P.I.","It replaced the Dino 246 in 1975.","I am the V8 Ferrari that starred in the TV show Magnum, P.I.","Ferrari 308 GTB/GTS"],
    ["Porsche 911 Turbo (930)","Porsche",1975,"DE","supercar","3.0-litre turbo flat-six",256,155,5.5,1195,null,"Porsche added a turbocharger to the 911 and created one of the fastest cars of the 1970s. It has wide wheel arches and a big 'whale tail' rear wing. It was famous for being tricky, because the turbo power arrived all at once.","When it came out in 1975 it was the fastest production car in Germany.","Its nickname in Britain was 'the widowmaker' because it could spin if driven carelessly.","I am the turbo 911 with the whale tail wing.","Porsche 911 (930)"],
    ["Lotus Esprit","Lotus",1976,"GB","sports","2.0-litre four-cylinder",160,138,8,898,10675,"A sharp, wedge-shaped Lotus sports car designed by Giorgetto Giugiaro. It was built in England from 1976 to 2004, getting more powerful over the years, with turbo and later V8 engines.","In The Spy Who Loved Me, James Bond drove an Esprit into the sea and it turned into a submarine.","In 2013 the real film car was bought at auction by Elon Musk.","In a James Bond film I drove into the sea and turned into a submarine.","Lotus Esprit"],
    ["Aston Martin V8 Vantage","Aston Martin",1977,"GB","gt","5.3-litre V8",375,170,5.3,null,534,"Called 'Britain's first supercar' when it came out in 1977. It was a big, muscular coupé with a powerful hand-built V8 and a top speed of 170 mph, making it faster than most Ferraris of its day.","Aston Martin did not publish its exact power output.","Timothy Dalton's James Bond drove a V8 Volante (convertible) in The Living Daylights.","I was hailed as Britain's first supercar in 1977.","Aston Martin V8 Vantage (1977)"],
    ["BMW M1","BMW",1978,"DE","homologation","3.5-litre straight-six",273,162,6,1300,453,"BMW's first mid-engined road car and the first car from its M (Motorsport) division. It was meant to be built with Lamborghini's help for racing, but the deal fell apart, so BMW finished it themselves.","BMW created a race series called Procar where Formula 1 drivers raced identical M1s.","Famous artist Andy Warhol painted an M1 race car as an 'Art Car'.","I am the first BMW M car, raced by Formula 1 drivers in my own series.","BMW M1"],
    ["McLaren MP4/1","McLaren",1981,"GB","race","3.0-litre V8 (Cosworth DFV)",null,null,null,null,10,"The Formula 1 car that changed racing. Designer John Barnard built its chassis from carbon fibre, which is light but very strong. Carbon fibre is now used in every F1 car and in many supercars.","John Watson won the 1981 British Grand Prix in an MP4/1.","Carbon fibre protected drivers so well that crashes became much safer.","I was the first Formula 1 car with a carbon-fibre chassis.","McLaren MP4/1"],
    ["Audi Sport Quattro","Audi",1984,"DE","homologation","2.1-litre turbo five-cylinder",302,155,4.8,1300,224,"A short-wheelbase version of the Audi Quattro, built to win rallies in Group B. The Quattro brought four-wheel drive to rallying and changed the sport for ever.","The Sport Quattro is shorter than the normal Quattro to make it turn faster.","Four-wheel drive gave much better grip on gravel, snow and mud.","I am the short Audi rally car that made four-wheel drive famous.","Audi Quattro"],
    ["Ferrari 288 GTO","Ferrari",1984,"IT","homologation","2.9-litre twin-turbo V8",394,189,4.9,1160,272,"Ferrari built the 288 GTO to race in Group B, a wild class for rally and racing cars. The races were cancelled, so it became a road car instead, with a twin-turbo V8. It led to the F40.","Ferrari needed to make 200 for the rules, but demand was so high they built 272.","Its engine sits lengthways, unlike the sideways engine in the 308.","I am a twin-turbo Ferrari built for Group B racing that never happened.","Ferrari 288 GTO"],
    ["Ferrari Testarossa","Ferrari",1984,"IT","supercar","4.9-litre flat-12",385,180,5.8,1506,7177,"The Ferrari of the 1980s: very wide, with big 'cheese grater' side strakes that feed air to the radiators. Its name means 'red head', after the red cam covers on its flat-12 engine.","A white Testarossa starred in the TV series Miami Vice.","It is wider at the back than at the front, because the radiators sit in the sides.","I am the 1980s Ferrari with 'cheese grater' sides and a red-headed engine.","Ferrari Testarossa"],
    ["Ford RS200","Ford",1984,"GB","homologation","1.8-litre turbo four-cylinder",247,147,5,1050,200,"A Ford built only for Group B rallying, with a turbo engine behind the seats and four-wheel drive. To be allowed to race, Ford had to build 200 road cars. The body was made of plastic and glass fibre.","Group B was cancelled after 1986 because the cars had become too fast and dangerous.","The RS200 was assembled in England.","I am Ford's Group B rally car, and 200 of me were built for the road.","Ford RS200"],
    ["Aston Martin V8 Vantage Zagato","Aston Martin",1986,"GB","gt","5.3-litre V8",432,186,4.8,1650,52,"A short, chunky coupé with a body by Zagato. Aston Martin promised it would reach 186 mph, and it was sold out before customers had even seen one.","Only 52 coupés were made.","It has a bulge on the bonnet to make room for the carburettors.","I am a 1980s Aston Martin with an Italian Zagato body and only 52 coupés made.","Aston Martin V8 Zagato"],
    ["Porsche 959","Porsche",1986,"DE","homologation","2.85-litre twin-turbo flat-six",444,197,3.7,1450,337,"The most high-tech car of the 1980s. It had four-wheel drive that changed how much power went to each end, twin turbos, and computer-controlled suspension. When launched it was the fastest road car in the world.","A 959 rally car won the tough Paris–Dakar desert rally in 1986.","Microsoft founder Bill Gates owned one, but it was stuck at US customs for years.","I am the high-tech 1980s Porsche that won the Paris–Dakar rally.","Porsche 959"],
    ["Ferrari F40","Ferrari",1987,"IT","supercar","2.9-litre twin-turbo V8",471,201,4.1,1254,1311,"Built to celebrate Ferrari's 40th birthday, the F40 was basically a race car for the road: twin turbos, a giant rear wing, no carpets, and windows you slide by hand. It was the last car approved by Enzo Ferrari.","It was the first production road car with a claimed top speed over 200 mph.","Its body is made from carbon fibre and Kevlar to keep it light.","I was built for Ferrari's 40th birthday and Enzo Ferrari approved me himself.","Ferrari F40"],
    ["Ruf CTR Yellowbird","Ruf",1987,"DE","supercar","3.4-litre twin-turbo flat-six",463,211,4.1,1150,29,"Ruf is a small German company that rebuilds Porsche 911s. Its CTR, nicknamed Yellowbird, was so fast that in 1987 it beat all the world's supercars in a top-speed test by an American magazine, reaching 211 mph.","A famous video showed it drifting around the Nürburgring.","Most were made by converting customers' own Porsches.","I am a yellow Porsche-based car that beat every supercar in a 1987 speed test.","Ruf CTR"],
    ["Nissan Skyline GT-R (R32)","Nissan",1989,"JP","homologation","2.6-litre twin-turbo straight-six",276,155,null,1430,43937,"A small Japanese coupé that was almost unbeatable in touring car racing. Its twin-turbo straight-six and clever four-wheel drive made it so dominant in Australia that people called it 'Godzilla'.","Japanese car makers had agreed not to claim more than 276 bhp (280 PS), but many GT-Rs had more.","It is a hero in video games like Gran Turismo.","I am the Japanese 'Godzilla' that dominated touring car racing.","Nissan Skyline GT-R"],
    ["Honda NSX","Honda",1990,"JP","supercar","3.0-litre V6",270,168,null,1365,18000,"Honda's supercar that you could drive every day. It had the first all-aluminium body on a production car and a V6 that loved to rev. Formula 1 world champion Ayrton Senna helped test it.","Senna's feedback at the Nürburgring helped Honda make the body stiffer.","It made supercar makers realise their cars should be reliable and easy to drive too.","I am the Honda supercar that Ayrton Senna helped to test.","Honda NSX (first generation)"],
    ["Lamborghini Diablo","Lamborghini",1990,"IT","supercar","5.7-litre V12",485,202,4.5,1576,null,"The Countach's successor, and the first Lamborghini that could top 200 mph. It kept the scissor doors and V12, and later versions added four-wheel drive.","'Diablo' means devil in Spanish, after a famous fighting bull.","Marcello Gandini, who drew the Miura and Countach, designed the first sketches.","I am the 1990s Lamborghini named after the devil, and the first to beat 200 mph.","Lamborghini Diablo"],
    ["Vector W8","Vector",1990,"US","supercar","6.0-litre twin-turbo V8",625,218,3.8,1506,null,"An American supercar that looks like a stealth fighter plane. Its twin-turbo V8 sat behind the driver and the dashboard looked like a jet cockpit, with screens and switches.","Its makers used ideas and materials from the aerospace industry.","Very few were made before the company ran into money trouble.","I am the American supercar that looks like a stealth fighter jet.","Vector W8"],
    ["Bugatti EB110","Bugatti",1991,"IT","supercar","3.5-litre quad-turbo V12",553,213,4.5,1620,139,"A comeback for the famous Bugatti name, built in a brand-new factory in Italy. It had a V12 with four turbochargers and four-wheel drive, making it one of the most advanced cars of the early 1990s.","It was revealed in 1991 on the 110th birthday of Ettore Bugatti, the company's founder.","Formula 1 champion Michael Schumacher bought a yellow one.","I am a quad-turbo Bugatti built in Italy and named for Ettore Bugatti's 110th birthday.","Bugatti EB110"],
    ["Dodge Viper","Dodge",1992,"US","sports","8.0-litre V10",400,165,4.2,1490,null,"America's answer to the AC Cobra: a huge 8.0-litre V10 engine, a simple open body and almost no electronic help. The first cars didn't even have proper door handles or windows.","The V10 engine was developed with help from Lamborghini, which was owned by Chrysler at the time.","The side exhaust pipes got so hot they could burn your leg.","I am the American sports car with a huge 8.0-litre V10.","Dodge Viper"],
    ["Jaguar XJ220","Jaguar",1992,"GB","supercar","3.5-litre twin-turbo V6",542,212,3.8,1470,281,"Shown in 1988 as a V12 four-wheel-drive concept, the XJ220 went on sale in 1992 with a twin-turbo V6 and rear-wheel drive instead, which upset some buyers. It was still the fastest car in the world for a while.","It was built by Jaguar and the racing company TWR.","Its name came from the target top speed of 220 mph.","I am a British supercar named after a top speed of 220 mph.","Jaguar XJ220"],
    ["McLaren F1","McLaren",1992,"GB","supercar","6.1-litre V12 (BMW)",618,240,3.2,1138,106,"Designed by Gordon Murray, the McLaren F1 was the fastest production car in the world for years, reaching 240 mph in 1998. The driver sits in the middle with a passenger seat on each side, and the engine bay is lined with real gold.","Gold is great at reflecting heat, which is why it lines the BMW V12's engine bay.","A race version won Le Mans at its first try in 1995.","My driver sits in the middle, and my engine bay is lined with gold.","McLaren F1"],
    ["Aston Martin DB7","Aston Martin",1994,"GB","gt","3.2-litre supercharged straight-six",335,165,5.8,1750,7000,"The car that saved Aston Martin. Designed by Ian Callum, the DB7 was more affordable than earlier Astons and sold in big numbers, which helped the company survive in the 1990s.","It was built in a former Jaguar factory, because Ford owned both brands.","It was the most-produced Aston Martin of its time.","I am the Ian Callum Aston Martin that saved the company in the 1990s.","Aston Martin DB7"],
    ["Ferrari F50","Ferrari",1995,"IT","supercar","4.7-litre V12",512,202,3.8,1230,349,"Ferrari's 50th-birthday car used a V12 engine based on its 1990 Formula 1 engine, bolted straight to the carbon-fibre chassis like a race car. It came with a removable roof.","Ferrari made just 349, one fewer than it thought it could sell.","Because the engine is bolted to the chassis, you can feel it buzzing through the whole car.","I am Ferrari's 50th-birthday car with a V12 from Formula 1.","Ferrari F50"],
    ["Ferrari 550 Maranello","Ferrari",1996,"IT","gt","5.5-litre V12",478,199,4.4,1774,3083,"After 20 years of mid-engined flagships, Ferrari went back to a V12 in the front. The 550 was fast but comfortable enough for long trips.","It is named after Maranello, the Italian town where Ferraris are made.","Racing versions won their class at Le Mans in 2003.","I am the 1990s Ferrari that put the V12 back in the front.","Ferrari 550"],
    ["Lotus Elise","Lotus",1996,"GB","sports","1.8-litre four-cylinder",118,127,5.8,725,null,"A tiny, very light sports car that brought Lotus back to Colin Chapman's idea: 'simplify, then add lightness'. Its chassis is made of glued aluminium sections, a clever new idea.","It is named after Elisa, the granddaughter of Lotus's owner at the time, Romano Artioli.","It was made for 25 years, from 1996 to 2021.","I am the light little Lotus named after the boss's granddaughter, Elisa.","Lotus Elise"],
    ["TVR Cerbera","TVR",1996,"GB","gt","4.2-litre V8",360,185,4.1,1100,null,"A wild British sports car from Blackpool. TVR designed its own V8 engine for it, and the Cerbera had no anti-lock brakes or traction control, just raw power.","Its name comes from Cerberus, the three-headed dog from Greek myths.","The door buttons were hidden under the mirrors.","I am a TVR from Blackpool named after a three-headed dog.","TVR Cerbera"],
    ["Porsche 911 GT1","Porsche",1997,"DE","homologation","3.2-litre twin-turbo flat-six",537,191,3.9,1150,25,"A Le Mans racing car that had to be sold for the road. Despite the name, it shares very little with a normal 911. A GT1 won Le Mans overall in 1998.","The road version is called the 'Straßenversion', German for 'street version'.","Its engine is mounted in the middle, unlike a normal 911.","I am a Le Mans racer called 911 that won the race in 1998.","Porsche 911 GT1"],
    ["Ascari Ecosse","Ascari",1998,"GB","supercar","4.4-litre V8 (BMW)",420,200,4.1,1250,17,"A British supercar from the small Ascari company. It had a BMW V8 engine and a light composite body. The company was founded by Dutch businessman Klaas Zwart.","The company is named after Alberto Ascari, a 1950s Formula 1 world champion.","Only 17 were made.","I am a rare British supercar named after a 1950s F1 champion.","Ascari Ecosse"],
    ["Mercedes-Benz CLK GTR","Mercedes-Benz",1998,"DE","homologation","6.9-litre V12",604,205,3.8,1440,26,"Mercedes built this car to win the FIA GT Championship. The rules said road cars had to be built too, so 20 coupés and later a few roadsters were made, with a 6.9-litre V12.","It won the FIA GT Championship in 1997.","When new, it was one of the most expensive cars you could buy.","I am a Mercedes GT1 racer that was also built for the road.","Mercedes-Benz CLK GTR"],
    ["Pagani Zonda","Pagani",1999,"IT","supercar","6.0-litre V12 (Mercedes)",389,185,4,1250,140,"Horacio Pagani moved from Argentina to Italy with a dream of building his own supercar. The Zonda was the result: a carbon-fibre body, a Mercedes-AMG V12, and amazing details like a quad exhaust in a circle.","It is named after a warm wind that blows in Argentina.","The first version was the C12, shown at the Geneva Motor Show in 1999.","I am Horacio Pagani's first car, named after a wind in Argentina.","Pagani Zonda"],
    ["Noble M12","Noble",2000,"GB","sports","2.5-litre twin-turbo V6",310,165,4.1,1080,null,"A light, fast British sports car designed by Lee Noble. It had a twin-turbo V6 engine and a body made of glass fibre. Many were built as kit-style racing cars too.","Noble cars are made in Leicestershire, England.","It famously had no anti-lock brakes or traction control at first.","I am Lee Noble's twin-turbo British sports car from Leicestershire.","Noble M12"],
    ["Saleen S7","Saleen",2000,"US","supercar","7.0-litre V8",550,220,3.3,1300,100,"America's first true mid-engined supercar of the 2000s. It had a 7.0-litre V8, a carbon-fibre body and a race version that won many GT races.","Steve Saleen started by tuning Ford Mustangs.","A twin-turbo version had even more power.","I am a hand-built American supercar with a 7.0-litre V8.","Saleen S7"],
    ["Spyker C8","Spyker",2000,"NL","supercar","4.2-litre V8 (Audi)",400,187,4.5,1275,null,"A Dutch supercar with an aircraft theme. Spyker built planes a hundred years ago, so its cars have a propeller logo, a cockpit full of polished aluminium, and a gear lever with the linkage on show.","Its motto is 'Nulla tenaci invia est via', Latin for 'For the tenacious, no road is impassable'.","Victor Muller led the company when the C8 was made.","I am a Dutch supercar with a propeller badge and a jewel-like cockpit.","Spyker C8"],
    ["Aston Martin Vanquish","Aston Martin",2001,"GB","gt","5.9-litre V12",460,190,5,1835,2578,"A big V12 grand tourer with a carbon-fibre and aluminium frame and paddle shifters, like an F1 car. It was one of the first road cars to use paddles.","In the Bond film Die Another Day, it had 'adaptive camouflage' that made it invisible.","It was designed by Ian Callum.","In a Bond film I could turn invisible.","Aston Martin Vanquish"],
    ["Bentley Speed 8","Bentley",2001,"GB","race","4.0-litre twin-turbo V8",600,null,null,900,6,"A Le Mans prototype race car with a twin-turbo V8. In 2003 it won the 24 Hours of Le Mans, Bentley's first win there since 1930.","Speed 8s finished first and second at Le Mans in 2003.","The 'Bentley Boys' won Le Mans five times in the 1920s.","I won Le Mans for Bentley in 2003, its first win since 1930.","Bentley Speed 8"],
    ["Lamborghini Murciélago","Lamborghini",2001,"IT","supercar","6.2-litre V12",572,205,3.8,1746,4099,"The first new Lamborghini made under Audi's ownership. It had a V12, four-wheel drive and scissor doors, plus air intakes that open up by themselves when the engine gets hot.","It is named after a brave fighting bull that survived 24 sword strokes in 1879.","The last version, the LP 670-4 SuperVeloce, was lighter and more powerful.","I am the first Lamborghini made under Audi, with air scoops that pop open.","Lamborghini Murciélago"],
    ["Ferrari Enzo","Ferrari",2002,"IT","hypercar","6.0-litre V12",651,221,3.65,1365,400,"Named after Ferrari's founder, the Enzo used lessons from Formula 1, where Michael Schumacher was winning everything for Ferrari. Its nose looks like an F1 car and its V12 screams to 8,000 rpm.","Ferrari built 400, plus one extra which was given to Pope John Paul II and sold for charity.","It has carbon-ceramic brakes, which were new for road cars then.","I am the Ferrari hypercar named after Enzo himself, with a nose like an F1 car.","Ferrari Enzo"],
    ["Koenigsegg CC8S","Koenigsegg",2002,"SE","supercar","4.7-litre supercharged V8",655,240,3.5,1175,6,"The first car from Koenigsegg, Christian von Koenigsegg's company in Sweden. It had a supercharged V8 and a roof panel that can be stored under the front bonnet. Only six were made.","Its doors swing forward and up, a Koenigsegg trademark called 'dihedral synchro-helix'.","Christian started the company in 1994 when he was just 22.","I am the very first Koenigsegg, and only six of me were built.","Koenigsegg CC8S"],
    ["Bentley Continental GT","Bentley",2003,"GB","gt","6.0-litre twin-turbo W12",552,198,4.8,2350,null,"A big, luxurious coupé with a 6.0-litre W12 engine and four-wheel drive that could go nearly 200 mph. It was a huge success and is still made in new versions today.","A W12 engine is like two V6 engines joined together, making a W shape.","In 2022 Bentley used it as the base for the Batur, a hand-built coupé limited to 18 cars.","I am a luxury Bentley coupé with a W12 engine that can cross Europe in comfort.","Bentley Continental GT"],
    ["Lamborghini Gallardo","Lamborghini",2003,"IT","supercar","5.0-litre V10",493,192,4.2,1430,14022,"The 'baby Lambo' with a V10 engine and four-wheel drive. It was easier to drive than older Lamborghinis and became the best-selling Lamborghini of its time.","Italian police used Gallardos as patrol cars, including one that carried organs for transplant.","It is named after a famous breed of fighting bull.","I am the V10 'baby Lambo' that Italian police drove on patrol.","Lamborghini Gallardo"],
    ["Mercedes-Benz SLR McLaren","Mercedes-Benz",2003,"DE","gt","5.4-litre supercharged V8",617,208,3.8,1768,2157,"Mercedes and McLaren built this grand tourer together. It has a supercharged V8 at the front, butterfly doors, and an air brake that flips up when you brake hard.","It was built at McLaren's factory in Woking, England.","Its long nose and side exhausts were inspired by 1950s Mercedes racing cars.","I am a Mercedes built by McLaren in Woking, with an air brake that flips up.","Mercedes-Benz SLR McLaren"],
    ["Aston Martin DB9","Aston Martin",2004,"GB","gt","5.9-litre V12",450,186,4.9,1760,16500,"A beautiful V12 grand tourer designed by Henrik Fisker and Ian Callum. It was the first car built at Aston Martin's new factory in Gaydon, England.","Its doors swing slightly upwards, called 'swan doors', so they don't hit kerbs.","It was made for 12 years, from 2004 to 2016.","I am the Aston Martin with 'swan doors' that opened the Gaydon factory.","Aston Martin DB9"],
    ["Maserati MC12","Maserati",2004,"IT","homologation","6.0-litre V12",621,205,3.8,1335,50,"A Maserati built so that a racing version was allowed to compete in GT racing. It is based on the Ferrari Enzo, but longer and wider. The race car won the FIA GT Championship many times.","Only 50 road cars were made.","It is so long that it has a removable roof to make it easier to store.","I am a Maserati based on the Ferrari Enzo, built to go GT racing.","Maserati MC12"],
    ["Noble M400","Noble",2004,"GB","supercar","3.0-litre twin-turbo V6",425,187,3.2,1060,null,"A lighter, more powerful version of the Noble M12. It is named after its power-to-weight ratio: about 400 horsepower for every tonne.","It has no power steering and no anti-lock brakes.","Top Gear praised it as one of the best driver's cars of its time.","My name comes from having about 400 horsepower for every tonne.","Noble M400"],
    ["Porsche Carrera GT","Porsche",2004,"DE","supercar","5.7-litre V10",604,205,3.9,1380,1270,"A V10 supercar whose engine was first designed for a Le Mans racer. It had a carbon-fibre chassis, a manual gearbox and a ceramic clutch, and its V10 sound is one of the best ever.","The gear knob is made of wood, a nod to the wooden gear knob of Porsche's 917 race car.","Its V10 was based on an engine meant for Formula 1 and Le Mans.","I am a Porsche with a V10 race engine and a wooden gear knob.","Porsche Carrera GT"],
    ["Ascari KZ1","Ascari",2005,"GB","supercar","5.0-litre V8 (BMW)",500,200,3.8,1330,50,"A British supercar named after the company's owner, Klaas Zwart (the K and Z). It had a BMW V8 engine and was built in Banbury, England. Only 50 were made.","Ascari's racing team won seven titles in the BOSS GP series.","The KZ1 was developed from the A10 racing car.","My name uses the initials of my company's owner, Klaas Zwart.","Ascari KZ1"],
    ["Bugatti Veyron","Bugatti",2005,"FR","hypercar","8.0-litre quad-turbo W16",987,253,2.5,1888,450,"The car that broke the 250 mph barrier. The Veyron had a W16 engine with four turbos and over 1,000 PS. Its Super Sport version set a record of 267.8 mph in 2010.","At full speed it would empty its fuel tank in about 12 minutes.","It needs a special key to unlock its top-speed mode.","I was the first road car with over 1,000 PS, and my engine has 16 cylinders.","Bugatti Veyron"],
    ["Ford GT","Ford",2005,"US","supercar","5.4-litre supercharged V8",550,205,3.8,1520,4038,"A modern remake of the GT40, built for Ford's 100th birthday. It looks like the old race car but is bigger, with a supercharged V8.","Ford couldn't call it GT40, because another company owned that name.","It was made from 2004 to 2006.","I am Ford's 2000s remake of the car that beat Ferrari at Le Mans.","Ford GT"],
    ["Gumpert Apollo","Gumpert",2005,"DE","supercar","4.2-litre twin-turbo V8 (Audi)",641,224,3,1100,null,"A German track-day supercar designed by Roland Gumpert, who used to lead Audi's rally team. It looks like a racing car and has a twin-turbo Audi V8.","Its makers said it made so much downforce that, in theory, it could drive upside down in a tunnel.","It was built in Altenburg, Germany.","In theory, I make enough downforce to drive upside down in a tunnel.","Gumpert Apollo"],
    ["Koenigsegg CCX","Koenigsegg",2006,"SE","supercar","4.7-litre twin-supercharged V8",795,245,3.2,1456,29,"A Koenigsegg designed to be sold around the world, including the USA. Its supercharged V8 could run on ethanol fuel for even more power.","CCX stands for 'Competition Coupé X', marking the 10th anniversary of the first CC prototype.","A CCX famously crashed on Top Gear's track, which led to a new rear wing.","I am the Koenigsegg made to go everywhere in the world, and my name has an X for 10 years.","Koenigsegg CCX"],
    ["Alfa Romeo 8C Competizione","Alfa Romeo",2007,"IT","gt","4.7-litre V8",444,181,4.2,1585,500,"A beautiful front-engined Alfa Romeo with a Maserati-built V8. It was inspired by the Alfa Romeo 33 Stradale and by racing Alfas of the 1930s and 40s.","Only 500 coupés were made, and 500 Spiders followed.","Its body is made of carbon fibre.","I am a curvy Alfa Romeo with a carbon body and only 500 coupés made.","Alfa Romeo 8C Competizione"],
    ["Audi R8","Audi",2007,"DE","supercar","4.2-litre V8",null,null,null,null,null,"Audi's first supercar, named after its Le Mans-winning race car. It had a mid-mounted engine, four-wheel drive and a 'side blade' panel behind the doors.","Tony Stark drove one in the first Iron Man film.","Its engine sits behind the seats under a glass cover so you can see it.","I am Audi's mid-engined supercar that Iron Man drove.","Audi R8"],
    ["Lamborghini Reventón","Lamborghini",2007,"IT","supercar","6.5-litre V12",641,211,3.4,1665,20,"A super-rare Lamborghini inspired by stealth fighter jets. It was based on the Murciélago with a new sharp body and a dashboard with aircraft-style screens.","Only 20 coupés were made for customers.","It is named after a bull that killed a famous bullfighter in 1943.","I am a Lamborghini inspired by stealth fighters, and only 20 of me were sold.","Lamborghini Reventón"],
    ["Nissan GT-R","Nissan",2007,"JP","supercar","3.8-litre twin-turbo V6",473,193,3.2,1740,null,"The modern 'Godzilla'. The GT-R used clever four-wheel drive and a fast-shifting gearbox to keep up with supercars that cost much more. Its twin-turbo V6 is built by hand.","Each engine is built by a single 'Takumi' craftsman, who puts a plate with their name on it.","It was made from 2007 to 2025, getting faster almost every year.","I am the modern 'Godzilla', and each of my engines is built by one craftsman.","Nissan GT-R"],
    ["SSC Ultimate Aero","SSC",2007,"US","hypercar","6.3-litre twin-turbo V8",1183,256,2.8,1247,24,"A small American company called SSC built this car with a twin-turbo V8. In 2007 it was officially the fastest production car in the world at 256 mph, beating the Bugatti Veyron.","SSC stands for Shelby SuperCars, but it is not connected to Carroll Shelby.","The record was set on a closed road in Washington State.","In 2007 I beat the Bugatti Veyron to become the fastest production car.","SSC Ultimate Aero"],
    ["Aston Martin One-77","Aston Martin",2009,"GB","hypercar","7.3-litre V12",750,220,3.5,1630,77,"A hand-built hypercar with a huge 7.3-litre V12 and a carbon-fibre chassis. Its aluminium body panels were shaped by hand.","The name comes from it being one of 77.","Aston Martin said it was the most powerful naturally aspirated road car in the world when it came out.","My name says it: I am one of only 77.","Aston Martin One-77"],
    ["Ferrari 458 Italia","Ferrari",2009,"IT","supercar","4.5-litre V8",562,202,3.4,1565,null,"A beautiful V8 Ferrari with an engine that screams to 9,000 rpm. Racing driver Michael Schumacher helped with its development, and its steering wheel holds the indicator and wiper buttons, like an F1 car.","Its front grille has small 'winglets' that bend at speed to reduce drag.","It was one of the last non-turbo V8 Ferraris.","I am a V8 Ferrari that revs to 9,000 rpm, with flexible winglets in my nose.","Ferrari 458"],
    ["Lotus Evora","Lotus",2009,"GB","sports","3.5-litre V6",276,162,5.1,1382,null,"A Lotus sports car with room for 2+2 (two adults plus two small rear seats). It had a Toyota V6 in the middle and was designed to be comfortable as well as fun.","Its body is made from aluminium and composite panels.","It was built in Hethel, Norfolk.","I am the 2+2 Lotus with a Toyota V6.","Lotus Evora"],
    ["Lexus LFA","Lexus",2010,"JP","supercar","4.8-litre V10",553,202,3.7,1480,500,"Toyota's luxury brand spent around ten years developing the LFA. Its V10 engine revs so quickly that a normal needle dial couldn't keep up, so it has a digital rev counter. Many people think it has the best engine sound of any car.","Its V10 can go from idle to its 9,000 rpm limit in about 0.6 seconds.","Yamaha's musical instrument experts helped tune the engine's sound.","My V10 revs so fast that I needed a digital rev counter, and Yamaha tuned my sound.","Lexus LFA"],
    ["Mercedes-Benz SLS AMG","Mercedes-Benz",2010,"DE","gt","6.2-litre V8",563,197,3.8,1620,null,"A modern take on the famous 1950s Mercedes 300 SL 'Gullwing'. Its doors open upwards like a seagull's wings, and a big 6.2-litre V8 sits at the front.","It was the first car designed completely by AMG, Mercedes' performance division.","An electric version, the SLS AMG Electric Drive, had four motors.","My doors open upwards like a seagull's wings.","Mercedes-Benz SLS AMG"],
    ["Noble M600","Noble",2010,"GB","supercar","4.4-litre twin-turbo V8",650,225,3,1250,null,"A British supercar with a twin-turbo V8 and a switch that lets you choose how much power you get. It was praised for being a pure, old-school driver's car with a manual gearbox.","Its 4.4-litre V8 started as a Volvo engine, built by Yamaha.","Like other Nobles, it is built in Leicestershire.","I am a British supercar with a Volvo-based V8 and a manual gearbox.","Noble M600"],
    ["Hennessey Venom GT","Hennessey",2011,"US","hypercar","7.0-litre twin-turbo V8",1244,270,2.7,1244,13,"An American hypercar built by Hennessey from a Lotus Exige chassis, made longer and fitted with a twin-turbo V8. It reached 270.49 mph at NASA's Kennedy Space Center shuttle runway in 2014.","It weighed about 1,244 kg and had about 1,244 bhp, so it had one horsepower for every kilo.","Only 13 were built, including the open-top Spyders.","I reached 270 mph on the Space Shuttle runway in Florida.","Hennessey Venom GT"],
    ["Lamborghini Aventador","Lamborghini",2011,"IT","supercar","6.5-litre V12",690,217,2.9,1575,11465,"A flagship V12 Lamborghini with scissor doors and a carbon-fibre tub. Its angular shape was inspired by stealth jets, and it was made for over ten years.","It is named after a fighting bull that won a trophy for bravery in 1993.","Its V12 was brand-new, the first new Lamborghini V12 since the 1960s.","I am the V12 Lamborghini named after a brave bull from 1993.","Lamborghini Aventador"],
    ["McLaren 12C","McLaren",2011,"GB","supercar","3.8-litre twin-turbo V8",592,207,3.3,1434,null,"McLaren's first road car after the F1, made at its new factory in Woking. It had a carbon-fibre tub, a twin-turbo V8 and clever suspension with no anti-roll bars.","Its carbon-fibre tub weighs only about 75 kg.","It was first called the MP4-12C, after McLaren's Formula 1 car names.","I am the McLaren that started its modern road-car range in 2011.","McLaren 12C"],
    ["Pagani Huayra","Pagani",2011,"IT","hypercar","6.0-litre twin-turbo V12 (Mercedes-AMG)",720,238,3.2,1350,100,"Horacio Pagani's second hypercar has small flaps at the front and back that move by themselves, like a bird's wings, to keep it stable. Its gull-wing doors open upwards.","Its name comes from Huayra-tata, an Andean god of wind.","It even uses titanium bolts, each with the Pagani name on it.","I am named after an ancient wind god, and my flaps move like wings.","Pagani Huayra"],
    ["Alfa Romeo 4C","Alfa Romeo",2013,"IT","sports","1.75-litre turbo four-cylinder",237,160,4.5,940,null,"A small, light sports car with a carbon-fibre tub, which was rare in such an affordable car. Its turbo four-cylinder engine sits behind the seats.","It has no power steering, so you can feel the road through the wheel.","4C stands for its four-cylinder engine.","I am a little Alfa Romeo with a carbon-fibre tub and four cylinders.","Alfa Romeo 4C"],
    ["LaFerrari","Ferrari",2013,"IT","hypercar","6.3-litre V12 hybrid",950,217,2.6,1585,499,"Ferrari's first hybrid hypercar, part of the 'holy trinity' with the McLaren P1 and Porsche 918. It used an F1-style energy recovery system (called HY-KERS) and a V12.","Its name means 'The Ferrari', because Ferrari saw it as the ultimate expression of the brand.","The seat is fixed to the chassis; instead, the pedals and steering wheel move to fit the driver.","My name simply means 'The Ferrari', and I am a hybrid with a V12.","LaFerrari"],
    ["McLaren P1","McLaren",2013,"GB","hypercar","3.8-litre twin-turbo V8 hybrid",903,217,2.8,1395,375,"One of the 'holy trinity' of hybrid hypercars, with the LaFerrari and Porsche 918. It combined a twin-turbo V8 with an electric motor, using ideas from Formula 1 like a drag reduction system (DRS) on its rear wing.","Its rear wing can rise by 300 mm in Race mode.","The electric motor fills in gaps while the turbos build up boost.","I am McLaren's hybrid hypercar, part of the 'holy trinity'.","McLaren P1"],
    ["Porsche 918 Spyder","Porsche",2013,"DE","hypercar","4.6-litre V8 hybrid",875,214,2.6,1720,918,"A plug-in hybrid hypercar with a V8 and two electric motors. In 2013 it became the first road car to lap the Nürburgring in under 7 minutes.","Exactly 918 were built, matching its name.","Its exhausts point straight up out of the engine cover.","I am the hybrid Porsche, and exactly 918 of me were built.","Porsche 918 Spyder"],
    ["Rimac Concept One","Rimac",2013,"HR","hypercar","4 electric motors",1073,221,2.5,1850,8,"The first car from Rimac, a company started in Croatia by Mate Rimac. It was one of the world's first electric hypercars, with four motors that could control each wheel separately.","Mate Rimac started by turning his old BMW into an electric car in his garage.","Only 8 were built.","I am one of the first electric hypercars, built in Croatia.","Rimac Concept One"],
    ["Lamborghini Huracán","Lamborghini",2014,"IT","supercar","5.2-litre V10",602,202,3.2,1422,null,"The V10 Lamborghini that replaced the Gallardo. It became the best-selling Lamborghini ever up to that time, with many versions including the off-road Sterrato.","Its name comes from a fighting bull from 1879.","The Huracán Performante used moving air channels to help it set lap records.","I am the V10 Lamborghini with an off-road version called Sterrato.","Lamborghini Huracán"],
    ["Aston Martin Vulcan","Aston Martin",2015,"GB","race","7.0-litre V12",820,null,null,1350,24,"A track-only Aston Martin with a 7.0-litre V12. It isn't road legal, so owners join special track days where Aston Martin teaches them how to drive it.","It is named after the Avro Vulcan, a British bomber plane.","One car was later converted to be road legal by a specialist company.","I am a track-only Aston Martin named after a British bomber plane.","Aston Martin Vulcan"],
    ["Koenigsegg Agera RS","Koenigsegg",2015,"SE","hypercar","5.0-litre twin-turbo V8",1160,278,2.8,1395,25,"In 2017 the Agera RS became the fastest production car in the world, averaging 277.9 mph on a closed public road in Nevada, USA. It also set records for 0–400–0 km/h.","'Agera' is a Swedish word meaning 'to act' or 'take action'.","Its ghost logo honours the jet fighter squadron that used the Koenigsegg factory buildings before.","In 2017 I averaged almost 278 mph on a closed road in Nevada.","Koenigsegg Agera"],
    ["Bugatti Chiron","Bugatti",2016,"FR","hypercar","8.0-litre quad-turbo W16",1479,261,2.4,1996,500,"The Veyron's successor, with a quad-turbo W16 engine making 1,500 PS. It is limited to 420 km/h on the road, which is still about 261 mph.","It is named after Louis Chiron, a racing driver from Monaco who drove for Bugatti.","It has a C-shaped curve on its sides, a nod to Bugatti design history.","I am named after a Monaco racing driver, and my W16 makes 1,500 PS.","Bugatti Chiron"],
    ["Honda NSX (2016)","Honda",2016,"JP","supercar","3.5-litre twin-turbo V6 hybrid",573,191,2.9,1796,null,"The second NSX is a hybrid supercar with a twin-turbo V6 and three electric motors: one behind the engine and one for each front wheel, which helps it turn into corners.","It was designed and built in Ohio, USA.","In North America it was sold as the Acura NSX.","I am a hybrid Honda with an electric motor for each front wheel, built in Ohio.","Honda NSX (second generation)"],
    ["Koenigsegg Regera","Koenigsegg",2016,"SE","hypercar","5.0-litre twin-turbo V8 hybrid",1479,250,2.8,1590,80,"A luxury hybrid hypercar with no normal gearbox. Instead, Koenigsegg's 'Direct Drive' system connects the engine straight to the wheels, with electric motors helping at low speeds.","'Regera' is Swedish for 'to reign'.","Its body can open and close all its panels by itself, like a robot.","I am a Koenigsegg with no gearbox, and my name means 'to reign'.","Koenigsegg Regera"],
    ["Ford GT (2017)","Ford",2017,"US","supercar","3.5-litre twin-turbo V6",647,216,3,1385,1350,"The second modern Ford GT, built to return to Le Mans. It has a twin-turbo V6 and 'flying buttresses' that guide air around the car. Exactly 50 years after the GT40's 1966 win, the race version won its class at Le Mans in 2016.","It was built by Multimatic in Canada.","Buyers had to apply, and Ford chose who could have one.","I won my class at Le Mans in 2016, 50 years after the GT40's famous win.","Ford GT"],
    ["McLaren 720S","McLaren",2017,"GB","supercar","4.0-litre twin-turbo V8",710,212,2.9,1419,null,"A twin-turbo V8 McLaren with a carbon-fibre tub and a striking 'eye socket' design that hides the headlights and the radiator air intakes.","Its dashboard screen can fold down to show only the most important information.","720S comes from its 720 PS.","My headlights sit inside 'eye sockets' that also feed air to my radiators.","McLaren 720S"],
    ["Apollo Intensa Emozione","Apollo",2018,"DE","hypercar","6.3-litre V12",769,208,2.7,1250,10,"A wild hypercar from Apollo, the company that took over from Gumpert. Its name means 'Intense Emotion'. It has a screaming V12 and a body covered in fins and vents.","Only 10 were made.","It has a carbon-fibre chassis inspired by Le Mans race cars.","My name means 'Intense Emotion', and I came from the company after Gumpert.","Apollo Intensa Emozione"],
    ["McLaren Senna","McLaren",2018,"GB","hypercar","4.0-litre twin-turbo V8",789,208,2.8,1198,500,"A track-focused McLaren named after Ayrton Senna, the three-time Formula 1 champion who won his titles driving for McLaren. Its huge rear wing and see-through door panels make it look like a racing car.","You can choose glass panels in the doors so you can see the track beside you.","Its rear wing moves to help with braking and cornering.","I am named after a three-time Formula 1 champion who drove for McLaren.","McLaren Senna"],
    ["Aston Martin Valhalla","Aston Martin",2019,"GB","hypercar","4.0-litre twin-turbo V8 hybrid",1064,217,2.5,1655,999,"A mid-engined plug-in hybrid from Aston Martin, with a twin-turbo V8 and three electric motors. It uses Formula 1 ideas to make downforce.","Valhalla is the hall of heroes in Norse myths.","It was first shown as a concept in 2019, and production began years later.","I am a hybrid Aston Martin named after the Norse hall of heroes.","Aston Martin Valhalla"],
    ["Bugatti Chiron Super Sport 300+","Bugatti",2019,"FR","hypercar","8.0-litre quad-turbo W16",1578,304,2.4,1996,30,"In 2019 a longer, low-drag version of the Bugatti Chiron became the first car to go faster than 300 mph, reaching 304.77 mph at Ehra-Lessien test track in Germany. Bugatti then built 30 road versions.","The record was set by racing driver Andy Wallace, who also won Le Mans in 1988.","The record run went in one direction only, so it didn't count as an official world record.","I was the first car to go faster than 300 mph.","Bugatti Chiron"],
    ["Ferrari SF90 Stradale","Ferrari",2019,"IT","hypercar","4.0-litre twin-turbo V8 plug-in hybrid",986,211,2.5,1570,null,"Ferrari's first plug-in hybrid series car. A twin-turbo V8 works with three electric motors to make 1,000 PS. It can even drive a short distance on electricity alone, silently.","SF90 celebrates 90 years of Scuderia Ferrari, the racing team.","With electric front motors, it is a four-wheel-drive Ferrari.","I am a plug-in hybrid Ferrari that celebrates 90 years of its racing team.","Ferrari SF90 Stradale"],
    ["Koenigsegg Jesko Absolut","Koenigsegg",2019,"SE","hypercar","5.0-litre twin-turbo V8",1578,300,2.35,1420,125,"The lowest-drag Koenigsegg, designed for top speed. Its twin-turbo V8 makes up to 1,600 PS on E85 fuel, and it uses a 9-speed gearbox with seven clutches that can jump between gears.","The Jesko is named after Christian von Koenigsegg's father, Jesko.","In 2026 a Jesko Absolut set records for 0–100 km/h in 2.35 seconds and other sprint tests, independently timed.","I am named after Christian von Koenigsegg's father, and I am built for top speed.","Koenigsegg Jesko"],
    ["Lotus Evija","Lotus",2019,"GB","hypercar","4 electric motors",1973,200,3,1887,130,"Lotus's first electric hypercar, with four electric motors and about 2,000 PS. Large tunnels go right through the back of the car to let air flow through it.","Its name means 'the first in existence' or 'the living one'.","It was built in Hethel, England, home of Lotus.","I am Lotus's electric hypercar with tunnels right through my back.","Lotus Evija"],
    ["Pininfarina Battista","Pininfarina",2019,"IT","hypercar","4 electric motors",1874,222,1.9,2200,150,"An electric hypercar from Automobili Pininfarina, the car company of the famous Italian design house. It shares much of its technology with the Rimac Nevera.","It is named after Battista 'Pinin' Farina, who founded the design house in 1930.","Its battery pack is shaped like a T, running down the middle and behind the seats.","I am an Italian electric hypercar named after the founder of Pininfarina.","Pininfarina Battista"],
    ["Czinger 21C","Czinger",2020,"US","hypercar","2.9-litre twin-turbo V8 hybrid",1233,268,1.9,1250,80,"An American hybrid hypercar built in a new way: many parts are 3D-printed by computer-designed robots, making them strong and light. The driver and passenger sit one behind the other, like in a fighter jet.","Kevin Czinger started the company in Los Angeles.","Its V8 is only 2.88 litres but revs to 11,000 rpm.","My parts are 3D-printed, and my passenger sits behind me like in a fighter jet.","Czinger 21C"],
    ["Gordon Murray T.50","Gordon Murray Automotive",2020,"GB","supercar","3.9-litre V12 (Cosworth)",654,226,2.8,986,100,"Gordon Murray, designer of the McLaren F1, created the T.50 as its spiritual successor. It has a central driving seat, a Cosworth V12 that revs to 12,100 rpm, a manual gearbox, and a big fan at the back that sucks the car to the road.","It weighs under 1,000 kg, light for a modern supercar.","The fan idea comes from the Brabham BT46B Formula 1 car that Murray designed in 1978.","I have a fan at the back and a driver's seat in the middle, like the McLaren F1.","Gordon Murray Automotive T.50"],
    ["Hennessey Venom F5","Hennessey",2020,"US","hypercar","6.6-litre twin-turbo V8",1817,311,2.6,1385,24,"A hypercar designed from scratch by Hennessey in Texas, aiming for over 300 mph. Its twin-turbo 6.6-litre V8 is nicknamed 'Fury'.","F5 is the strongest type of tornado, with winds over 260 mph.","Only 24 coupés were planned.","I am named after the strongest kind of tornado.","Hennessey Venom F5"],
    ["Koenigsegg Gemera","Koenigsegg",2020,"SE","hypercar","2.0-litre three-cylinder hybrid",1400,249,1.9,1850,300,"Koenigsegg calls it the world's first four-seat hypercar: a 'Mega-GT' with room for four adults and luggage. The first version used a tiny three-cylinder engine plus electric motors.","The little engine is nicknamed the 'Tiny Friendly Giant'.","Later Koenigsegg added a V8 hybrid option with even more power.","I am a four-seat hypercar with a tiny engine nicknamed 'Tiny Friendly Giant'.","Koenigsegg Gemera"],
    ["Maserati MC20","Maserati",2020,"IT","supercar","3.0-litre twin-turbo V6",621,202,2.9,1500,null,"Maserati's mid-engined supercar with its own Nettuno V6, which uses technology from Formula 1 called pre-chamber ignition. MC stands for Maserati Corse (racing), and 20 for 2020.","Its butterfly doors open upwards.","Nettuno means Neptune, the god of the sea, whose trident is on Maserati's badge.","My engine is named after Neptune, god of the sea.","Maserati MC20"],
    ["Aston Martin Valkyrie","Aston Martin",2021,"GB","hypercar","6.5-litre V12 hybrid (Cosworth)",1139,220,2.5,1355,150,"A road car designed with Formula 1 genius Adrian Newey. It has huge tunnels under the body to suck it to the road, and a Cosworth V12 that revs to over 11,000 rpm. A race version raced at Le Mans in 2025.","The driver sits with their feet up, like in a racing car.","The Valkyries are spirits from Norse myths who choose heroes in battle.","I was designed with Adrian Newey, and I race in the Le Mans Hypercar class.","Aston Martin Valkyrie"],
    ["Ferrari 296 GTB","Ferrari",2021,"IT","supercar","3.0-litre twin-turbo V6 hybrid",819,205,2.9,1470,null,"A plug-in hybrid Ferrari with a twin-turbo V6, the first six-cylinder Ferrari road car with a Prancing Horse badge since the Dino era. The engine is so smooth and high-revving it is nicknamed the 'little V12'.","296 comes from its 2.9-litre engine with 6 cylinders.","It can drive up to about 25 km on electricity alone.","I am a hybrid V6 Ferrari nicknamed the 'little V12'.","Ferrari 296"],
    ["Lamborghini Countach LPI 800-4","Lamborghini",2021,"IT","supercar","6.5-litre V12 hybrid",803,221,2.8,1595,112,"A modern tribute to the 1970s Countach for its 50th birthday. It has a V12 with a small electric motor powered by a supercapacitor (a battery that charges and empties very fast).","Only 112 were made, because the original Countach project was called LP112.","Its shape copies the original's wedge and its periscope-style roof.","I am a modern tribute to the 1970s poster car, and only 112 of me were made.","Lamborghini Countach LPI 800-4"],
    ["Lotus Emira","Lotus",2021,"GB","sports","3.5-litre supercharged V6",400,180,4.3,1487,null,"Lotus's last car powered only by petrol. It is a mid-engined sports car with a supercharged V6 or a four-cylinder turbo, and it was designed to be more comfortable than older Lotuses.","Its name means 'commander' or 'leader' in some ancient languages.","It was built at Hethel, where Lotus has made cars since 1966.","I am the last petrol-only Lotus.","Lotus Emira"],
    ["Rimac Nevera","Rimac",2021,"HR","hypercar","4 electric motors",1888,258,1.97,2300,150,"An all-electric hypercar from Croatia that broke more than 20 records, including fastest electric car at 258 mph. With four motors, it can launch to 60 mph in under 2 seconds.","It is named after a powerful, sudden Mediterranean storm.","Each wheel has its own motor, so the computer can control the grip of every wheel.","I am the electric Croatian hypercar that broke over 20 records.","Rimac Nevera"],
    ["Mercedes-AMG One","Mercedes-Benz",2022,"DE","hypercar","1.6-litre turbo V6 hybrid (from F1)",1049,219,2.9,1695,275,"A road car with a real Formula 1 engine: a 1.6-litre turbo V6 hybrid, from the Mercedes team that won many world titles, helped by electric motors. In 2024 it lapped the Nürburgring in 6:29.090, a record for production cars.","The engine needs to be rebuilt after about 50,000 km.","Its engine idles at about 1,200 rpm and revs to 11,000 rpm.","I am a road car with a real Formula 1 hybrid engine.","Mercedes-AMG One"],
    ["Pagani Utopia","Pagani",2022,"IT","hypercar","6.0-litre twin-turbo V12 (Mercedes-AMG)",852,null,null,1280,99,"Horacio Pagani's third hypercar, with a twin-turbo Mercedes-AMG V12 and, unusually, the choice of a manual gearbox. Pagani wanted it to be simple and beautiful, with no huge wings.","Only 99 coupés were made.","Its gear lever has an open metal linkage you can see working, like a mechanical watch.","I am Pagani's third hypercar, and you can choose a manual gearbox.","Pagani Utopia"],
    ["Alfa Romeo 33 Stradale (2023)","Alfa Romeo",2023,"IT","supercar","3.0-litre twin-turbo V6",612,206,3,1500,33,"A modern tribute to the 1967 33 Stradale, with butterfly doors and a shape that copies the original. Customers could choose a twin-turbo V6 or an all-electric version.","Only 33 were made, and they sold out before the car was even shown.","It was built with help from Maserati.","Only 33 of me were made, as a tribute to a 1960s Alfa Romeo.","Alfa Romeo 33 Stradale (2023)"],
    ["Ferrari 499P","Ferrari",2023,"IT","race","3.0-litre twin-turbo V6 hybrid",671,null,null,1030,null,"Ferrari's Le Mans Hypercar, with a twin-turbo V6 and electric motor driving the front wheels. It won the 24 Hours of Le Mans three years in a row, in 2023, 2024 and 2025.","Its 2023 win came 50 years after Ferrari last raced for the overall win at Le Mans, in 1973.","Toyota ended Ferrari's run of wins in June 2026.","I won Le Mans three times in a row, in 2023, 2024 and 2025.","Ferrari 499P"],
    ["Lamborghini Revuelto","Lamborghini",2023,"IT","hypercar","6.5-litre V12 plug-in hybrid",1001,217,2.5,1772,null,"The Aventador's successor: a V12 plug-in hybrid with three electric motors and over 1,000 PS. It can drive on electric power alone for a short distance.","Its name means 'mixed up' in Spanish, after a fighting bull, and it hints at mixing petrol and electric power.","It was Lamborghini's first plug-in hybrid series car.","I am a V12 hybrid Lamborghini, and my name means 'mixed up'.","Lamborghini Revuelto"],
    ["Bugatti Tourbillon","Bugatti",2024,"FR","hypercar","8.3-litre V16 hybrid",1775,276,2,1995,250,"The Chiron's successor, with a brand-new 8.3-litre V16 engine plus three electric motors. Its dashboard dials are made like a Swiss watch, with over 600 tiny parts.","A tourbillon is a mechanism in very fine watches.","Only 250 will be made.","I am a Bugatti with a V16 hybrid engine and a dashboard made like a Swiss watch.","Bugatti Tourbillon"],
    ["Ferrari F80","Ferrari",2024,"IT","hypercar","3.0-litre twin-turbo V6 hybrid",1184,217,2.15,1525,799,"Ferrari's newest flagship hypercar, using lessons from its Le Mans-winning 499P. A twin-turbo V6 and three electric motors give it 1,200 PS, the most powerful Ferrari road car ever.","It has a driver-focused cockpit where the passenger seat sits slightly back.","Only 799 were made, and they sold out at once.","I am the most powerful Ferrari road car ever, with 1,200 PS.","Ferrari F80"],
    ["Lamborghini Temerario","Lamborghini",2024,"IT","supercar","4.0-litre twin-turbo V8 hybrid",907,213,2.7,1690,null,"The Huracán's successor, a hybrid with a twin-turbo V8 that revs to 10,000 rpm plus three electric motors.","Its name comes from a fighting bull, and means 'reckless' or 'bold' in Spanish.","It replaced the V10 with a twin-turbo V8 for the first time.","I am the hybrid Lamborghini whose V8 revs to 10,000 rpm.","Lamborghini Temerario"],
    ["McLaren W1","McLaren",2024,"GB","hypercar","4.0-litre twin-turbo V8 hybrid",1258,217,2.7,1399,399,"McLaren's hybrid hypercar for the 2020s, following the F1 and P1. It has a twin-turbo V8 and an electric motor making 1,275 PS, and racing-car aerodynamics.","W1 stands for 'World Championships', remembering McLaren's F1 titles.","Only 399 were made.","I am McLaren's newest 'number one' hypercar, after the F1 and P1.","McLaren W1"],
    ["Lexus LFA Concept","Lexus",2025,"JP","concept","electric",null,null,null,null,null,"In December 2025 Lexus showed a new electric sports car concept and gave it the famous LFA name. It was first shown in August 2025 as the 'Sport Concept'. Lexus has not announced full performance figures.","It is a battery electric car, unlike the original LFA's V10.","The original LFA was made from 2010 to 2012.","I am an electric concept that brought back the LFA name in 2025.","Lexus LFA"]
];
